# The Role of Narrative in Understanding Digital Video: An Exploratory Analysis.

**Authors:** Wilkens, Todd, Hughes, Anthony, Wildemuth, Barbara M., Marchionini, Gary

## Abstract
Outlines the basic principles and research supporting the concept of narrative intelligence and its applicability to the ways in which people make sense of digital video. Explores relevant theory and research in sense-making, surrogates, narrative, and narrative intelligence and presents preliminary results of two research studies. Results have implications for how syntactic form can be used for indexing digital video. (Author/AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ679002

